n1 VERB/ACTION Executive SummaryAm nonsequi\ndolutatem reperit aspersp elendae consed ut magnita\nSCHOOL FOR\nconsedicitia audignatquo et iume nus et ad equibusBeris\nNATURE\nExecutive SummaryAm nonsequi dolutatem reperit aspersp elendae consed ut\nmagnita consedicitia audignatquo et iume nus et ad eos as eum ius, quibusFuga.\nFaccum quo quature pellitibus con con nonsequia alit, intem. Ut porro bla\nsunt porunt qui re dolorer fersperspe delignis quatem quas sus a cor solut fuga.\n1 VERB/ACTION Executive SummaryAm nonsequi\ndolutatem reperit aspersp elendae consed ut magnita\nconsedicitia audignatquo et iume nus et ad equibusBeris\nRATIONALE\nExecutive SummaryAm nonsequi dolutatem reperit aspersp elendae consed ut\nmagnita consedicitia audignatquo et iume nus et ad eos as eum ius, quibusFuga.\nFaccum quo quature pellitibus con con nonsequia alit, intem. Ut porro bla\nRewilding efforts have proven that recovery is possible, but scaling them to the continental level requires\nsunt porunt qui re dolorer fersperspe delignis quatem quas sus a cor solut fuga.\nsomething still missing: well-trained, well-articulated teams and visionary leaders capable of managing\necosystems and economies at scale. The Iberá Leadership School for Nature is designed to fill this gap as the\nfirst practice-based, on-site training center in Latin America dedicated to forming the next generation of\nconservation leaders.\nGOAL\nTo establish a practice-based, on-site school for project leaders and managers, combining experiential and\nreal-time training in:\n• Territorial and river basin management\n• Ecosystem restoration and rewilding\n• Governance and collaboration with local communities\n• Creation of regenerative economies\n53 53\nActivities\nAnnex IX Iberá Leadership School for Nature\nWHY IBERÁ\n• 201+ yearsV oEf rReBw/ilAdiCngT eIxOpNeri enEcex: escuucctievsesf ul Sspuemcimesa rreyinAtmro ducntoionnsse,q nuait ure-based tourism, and\ncommunitdyo tlruatnastfeomrm arteiponer.it aspersp el