ylasterina (Coelenterata: Hydrozoa). Biol. Antarct. Seas XIII 38, 61–164 (1983).\n21. Häussermann, V. & Försterra, G. Extraordinary abundance of hydrocorals (Cnidaria, Hydrozoa, Stylasteridae) in shallow water\nof the Patagonian fjord region. Polar Biol. 30(4), 487–492. https://d oi.o rg/1 0.1 007/s 00300-0 06-0 207-5 (2007).\n22. Häussermann, V. & Försterra, G. Vast reef-like accumulation of the hydrocoral Errina antarctica (Cnidaria, Hydrozoa) wiped out\nin Central Patagonia. Coral Reefs 33, 29 (2014).\n23. Thrush, S. F., Gray, J. S., Hewitt, J. E. & Ugland, K. I. Predicting the effects of habitat homogenization on marine biodiversity. Ecol.\nAppl. 16(5), 1636–1642 (2006).\n24. Díaz, S. & Cabido, M. Vive la différence: Plant functional diversity matters to ecosystem processes. Trends Ecol. Evol. 16(11),\n646–655. https://d oi.o rg/1 0.1 016/S 0169-5 347(01)0 2283-2 (2001).\n25. Scinto, A. et al. Role of Paramuricea clavata forest in modifying the coralligenous assemblages. In 1st Symposium Sur Le Coralligène\nEt Autre Bio Concrétionscalcaires 136–140 (2009).\n26. Cerrano, C. et al. Gold coral (Savala savaglia) and gorgonian forest enhance benthic biodiversity and ecosystem functioning in\nthe mesophotic zone. Biodivers. Conserv. 19(1), 153–167. https://d oi.o rg/1 0.1 007/s 10531-0 09-9 712-5 (2010).\n27. Van der Linden, P. et al. A biological trait approach to assess the functional composition of subtidal benthic communities in an\nestuarine ecosystem. Ecol. Ind. 20, 121–133 (2012).\n28. Clare, D., Robinson, L. A. & Frid, C. L. J. Community variability and ecological functioning: 40 years of change in the North Sea\nbenthos. Mar. Environ. Res. 107, 24–34 (2015).\n29. Häussermann V, Försterra G. Marine benthic fauna of Chilean Patagonia.: illustrated dentification guide. In Nature in Focus (eds.\nHáussermann, V. & Försterra, G.)1000 pp. Puerto Montt, Chile (2009).\n30. Friedlander, A. M. et al. Marine communities of the newly created Kawésqar National Reserve, Chile: From glaciers to the Pacific\nOcean. PLoS One 16(4), e0249413 (2021).\n31. Silva N, Palma S. Progress in the oceanographic knowledge of Chilean interior waters, from Puerto Montt to Cape Horn (ed.\nComité Oceanográfico Nacional) Pontificia Universidad Católica de Valparaíso, pp 161. (2008).\n32. Viale, M. & Garreaud, R. Orographic effects of the subtropical and extratropical Andes on upwind precipitating clouds. J. Geophys.\nRes. Atmos. 120, 4962–4974 (2015).\n33. Aguayo, R. et al. The glass half-empty: Climate change drives lower freshwater input in the coastal system of the Chilean Northern\nPatagonia. Clim. Change 155, 417–435 (2019).\n34. Pantoja, S., Iriarte, J. L. & Daneri, G. Oceanography of the Chilean Patagonia. Cont. Shelf Res. 31(3–4), 149–153. https://d oi.o rg/\n10.1 016/j.c sr.2 010.1 0.0 13 (2011).\n35. Antezana, T., Guglielmo, L. & Ghirardelli, E. Microbasins within the Strait of Magellan affecting zooplankton distribution. In\nOceanografía en Antártica, ENEA Proyecto Antarctica (eds Gallardo, V.A, Ferretti, O. & Moyano, H.I.) Ediciones Documentas,\n443–458 (1992).\n36. Kruskal, W. H. & Wallis, W. A. Use of ranks in one-criterion variance analysis. J. Am. Stat. Assoc. 47, 583–621 (1952).\n37. WoRMS Editorial Board. World Register of Marine Species. https://w ww.m arine speci es.o rg at VLIZ. Accessed 25 Apr (2023).\n38. Shannon, C. E. A mathematical theory of communication. Bell Syst. Techn. J. 27, 379–423 (1948).\n39. Oksanen J et al. Vegan: Community Ecology Package. R package version 2.6–4. https://C RAN.R-p rojec t.o rg/p ackag e=v egan (2022).\n40. Zuur, A. F. & Ieno, E. N. A protocol for conducting and presenting results of regression-type analyses. Methods Ecol. Evol. 7(6),\n636–645 (2016).\n41. Zaar, J. Biostatistical Analysis. In Prentice-Hall 4th edn 123 (Englewood Cliffs, NJ, 1999).\n42. Clarke, K. R. & Warwick, R. M. Change in marine communities. In An Approach to Statistical Analysis and Interpretation 2nd edn\n(PRIMER-E, Plymouth, 2