al extinctions – devastating global record\n38\nLesser Bilby (Macrotis leucura)\nPig-footed Bandicoot (Chaeropus ecaudatus)\nDesert Rat-kangaroo (Caloprymnus campestris)\nA National Biodiversity Crisis\nOngoing biodiversity decline\nIn one part of\nAustralia, much of\nwhat has been lost\nelsewhere remains.\nSource: Threatened Species Index (TSX), Australia (1985–2019)\nThe Kimberley\nKey stronghold for threatened and endemic species\nAustralian Wildlife Conservancy (AWC)\nMission\nThe effective conservation of\nall Australian animals and\ntheir habitats\nOpportunity for conservation at scale through collaboration\n25 years of AWC in the Kimberley\nBunuba and Kija Country – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nAWC Tenure\n2001\n320,000 ha\nPurple-crowned Fairywren – Nikki Teunissen/ AWC\nOpportunity for conservation at scale through collaboration\n25 years of AWC in the Kimberley\n2001\nMornington\n320,000\nhectares\nWilinggin Country – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nAWC Tenure\n2007\n570,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2001\n320,000 ha\nGouldian Finch – Martin Willis/ AWC\nOpportunity for conservation at scale through collaboration\n25 years of AWC in the Kimberley\nKija Country – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nAboriginal Partnership\n2012\n880,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2007\n570,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2001\n320,000 ha\nAgile Wallaby – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nOpportunity for conservation at scale through collaboration\n25 years of AWC in the Kimberley\nWilinggin Country – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nAWC Tenure\n2015\n1,180,000 ha\nAboriginal Partnership\n2012\n880,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2007\n570,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2001\n320,000 ha\nGolden Bandicoot – Tom Sayers/ AWC\nOpportunity for conservation at scale through collaboration\n25 years of AWC in the Kimberley\nGovernment Partnership\n2016\n1,750,000 ha\nDambimangari Country – Wayne Lawler/ AWC\nAWC Tenure\n2015\n1,180,000 ha\nAboriginal Partnership\n2012\n880,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2007\n570,000 ha\nAWC Tenure\n2001\n320,000 ha\nKimberley Brushtail Phascogale – Ian Bool/ AWC\nOpportunity for con